steps.body:
```java
public class Hello {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, Java!");
    }
}
```

- All code lives inside a **class**. A `public` class must sit in a file with the same name: `Hello.java`.
- `main` is the entry point. Statements end with `;`.
- Classic workflow: `javac Hello.java` compiles to bytecode, `java Hello` runs it. Since Java 11, `java Hello.java` does both in one step.

Java 25 trims this down even further — you'll see that later in the course.

