steps.body:
Files, sockets and database connections must be closed. Since Java 7, declare them in the `try` header and Java closes them for you — even if an exception is thrown:

```java
try (BufferedReader in = Files.newBufferedReader(Path.of("data.txt"))) {
    System.out.println(in.readLine());
} catch (IOException e) {
    System.err.println("Could not read: " + e.getMessage());
}
```

- Works with anything that implements `AutoCloseable`.
- Several resources are separated by `;` and closed in **reverse** order.
- Since Java 9 you can also list an existing effectively-final variable: `try (in) { ... }`.

