steps.body:
Previewed in 12 and 13, final in **14**:

```java
int n = 4;
String size = switch (n) {
    case 1, 2 -> "small";
    case 3, 4 -> "medium";
    default -> {
        String label = "large";
        yield label;
    }
};
```

- The switch **returns a value**, and must cover every case.
- Arrow labels **never fall through** — no `break` needed.
- Several labels per case: `case 1, 2`.
- `yield` returns a value from a block.

Java 14 also made **helpful NullPointerExceptions** the default: the message says which call failed and what was null.

